Keep sampled depth on the GPU, and add frame-pacing diagnostics.

A texture reading a depth target took a GPU wait, a full readback, a CPU
conversion and a texture re-upload whenever the depth was the bound target
or had only been cleared. WKC2 does both every frame (its 2560x2560 shadow
map and a cleared depth in the character creator). DEPTH24_D8 reads now use a
snapshot retaken after the last depth write, and a cleared target can be
snapshotted; the creator went from ~37 to a steady 60 fps.

Also added, off by default:
- RSX_ENGINE_ZTEX_GPU=1: re-encode a Z24S8 depth read as A8R8G8B8 on the GPU
  (compute pass; adds a compute stage to the HLSL->SPIR-V helper). Its output
  still blurs WKC2's depth of field, so the guest-memory path stays default.
- RSX_ENGINE_ZTEX_LOG=<file>: formats of depth targets sampled as textures.
- RSX_ENGINE_PRESENT_LOG: a "fresh" count beside fps -- presents whose surface
  some draw wrote since it was last shown.
- RSX_ENGINE_BURST_DIR=<dir> (+RSX_ENGINE_BURST_N): on <dir>/arm, write the
  next presented frames with present times.
- RSX_ENGINE_SNAP_EVERY_S accepts fractions of a second.
- PAD_FILE: a negative hold count is a hold in milliseconds, logged with
  start/end times to <PAD_FILE>.log.

